{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1176311-combining-touch-spells-and-unarmed-attacks","id":1176311,"title":"Combining touch spells and unarmed attacks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-15T10:02:19-08:00","id":1176311,"title":"Combining touch spells and unarmed attacks","content":"So this is probably in the book somewhere, but I'm not finding it.<br /> <br /> So let's say I'm casting a spell delivered by touch. Is it possible to combine that spell with an unarmed attack? I don't see a logical reason why you couldn't, but it also seems like the kind of thing that might fuck up the turn economy.<br /> <br /> Example: Punch Mage has encountered a Seer of the Throne, and so he's decided to do what he does best and punch and be mage. With his 3 dots in life, he casts Bruise Life, which does bashing damage equal to potency. He gives it a potency of 2. Punch Mage must now deliver his spell by touch, so he punches the seer of the throne in the face. He rolls 3 successes for 3 bashing damage and then gets an additional 2 from his spell. The Seer of the Throne probably has less than 5 stamina, so he is now beaten down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10984-neckbeard-the-pirate","name":"Neckbeard the Pirate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T11:21:30-08:00","id":1176332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neckbeard the Pirate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1176311-combining-touch-spells-and-unarmed-attacks#post1176311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So this is probably in the book somewhere, but I'm not finding it.<br /> <br /> So let's say I'm casting a spell delivered by touch. Is it possible to combine that spell with an unarmed attack? I don't see a logical reason why you couldn't, but it also seems like the kind of thing that might fuck up the turn economy.<br /> <br /> Example: Punch Mage has encountered a Seer of the Throne, and so he's decided to do what he does best and punch and be mage. With his 3 dots in life, he casts Bruise Life, which does bashing damage equal to potency. He gives it a potency of 2. Punch Mage must now deliver his spell by touch, so he punches the seer of the throne in the face. He rolls 3 successes for 3 bashing damage and then gets an additional 2 from his spell. The Seer of the Throne probably has less than 5 stamina, so he is now beaten down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Touch rules specifically say the touch does no damage. So you are only doing 2 damage via the spell via touch. You dont get to add the extra for punching. The not doing damage part is why its fine and doesnt break the turn economy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Lilith-Regular\">Touching an Opponent<br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Sometimes, a combatant doesn\u2019t want to do damage. Maybe<br /> she wants to plant a bug, or deliver a touch-range spell. Roll<br /> Dexterity + Brawl, or Dexterity + Weaponry to tap an opponent<br /> with a weapon. A successful roll deals no damage</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div> P219 2e Core","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 01-15-2018, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T12:17:56-08:00","id":1176343,"title":"","content":"Alternatively, there's always the Adamant Hand merit, if you have enough Reach to get the spell reflexively cast (or have the spell pre-cast with Time 2).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T12:34:48-08:00","id":1176351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1176311-combining-touch-spells-and-unarmed-attacks?p=1176332#post1176332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Touch rules specifically say the touch does no damage. So you are only doing 2 damage via the spell by touch. You dont get to add the extra for punching. The not doing damage part is why its fine and doesnt break the turn economy.<br /> <br /> P219 2e Core</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! Was looking all over for that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10984-neckbeard-the-pirate","name":"Neckbeard the Pirate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-15T23:36:22-08:00","id":1176473,"title":"","content":"Also: touching someone in combat is usually an instant action. Casting a spell also is. So when you cast the spell first, the spell is already gone the next round, when you touch your opponent, because the prerequisite of touching is not fulfilled. If you touch your opponent first, he will usually just move away before you can finish your spell the next turn. So for this to work in combat you would usually need to grapple someone and cast the spell in the grapple then.<br /> Other ways are as Knowbody point out to either hang the spell with time beforehand and deliver it with a punch/touch or cast reflexively while punching/touching. Either way, if you go for punching and hit, I don't see why you shouldn't do double damage with either of these ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T06:07:38-08:00","id":1176499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1176311-combining-touch-spells-and-unarmed-attacks?p=1176473#post1176473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also: touching someone in combat is usually an instant action. Casting a spell also is. So when you cast the spell first, the spell is already gone the next round, when you touch your opponent, because the prerequisite of touching is not fulfilled. If you touch your opponent first, he will usually just move away before you can finish your spell the next turn. So for this to work in combat you would usually need to grapple someone and cast the spell in the grapple then.<br /> Other ways are as Knowbody point out to either hang the spell with time beforehand and deliver it with a punch/touch or cast reflexively while punching/touching. Either way, if you go for punching and hit, I don't see why you shouldn't do double damage with either of these ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the touch rules dont state its a instant action","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T07:53:15-08:00","id":1176515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1176311-combining-touch-spells-and-unarmed-attacks?p=1176499#post1176499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, the touch rules dont state its a instant action</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither do they state it's a reflexive action, so I would go with the default as instant. Anyways as the text is written, it is clearly the intent of the authors that touching people and delivering spells that way should also be possible in combat, so I would allow it to be a reflexive action depending on the situation. I would e.g. not allow any yantras which need the use of your hands etc. and probably give you a malus, because the caster cannot use his hands freely while casting, since he needs those to actively touch his opponent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-16T08:20:16-08:00","id":1176518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1176311-combining-touch-spells-and-unarmed-attacks?p=1176515#post1176515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Neither do they state it's a reflexive action, so I would go with the default as instant. Anyways as the text is written, it is clearly the intent of the authors that touching people and delivering spells that way should also be possible in combat, so I would allow it to be a reflexive action depending on the situation. I would e.g. not allow any yantras which need the use of your hands etc. and probably give you a malus, because the caster cannot use his hands freely while casting, since he needs those to actively touch his opponent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its similar to throwing a spell with zero range (and no area) which is reflexive?<br /> <br /> Malus = minus? I think a minus is abit harsh as by default a mage doesnt need to use his hands for casting. (just mudras when applicable)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 01-16-2018, 12:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T01:28:33-08:00","id":1176720,"title":"","content":"Yeah you are right. Throwing a spell is reflexive so delivering it by touch should be, too. And yes malus is the opposite of bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T08:44:02-08:00","id":1176780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1176311-combining-touch-spells-and-unarmed-attacks?p=1176720#post1176720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah you are right. Throwing a spell is reflexive so delivering it by touch should be, too. And yes malus is the opposite of bonus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately touching an opponent is not reflexive (as stated in the touch rules), so you won't be able to use touch spells unless you have an effect (possibly through a Fighting Style, or a Time spell; otherwise by being in a grapple) that allows you to touch your opponent reflexively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T09:01:50-08:00","id":1176784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1176311-combining-touch-spells-and-unarmed-attacks?p=1176780#post1176780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unfortunately touching an opponent is not reflexive (as stated in the touch rules), so you won't be able to use touch spells unless you have an effect (possibly through a Fighting Style, or a Time spell; otherwise by being in a grapple) that allows you to touch your opponent reflexively.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats now how it reads and it doesnt actually say its not reflexive or that it uses an action. If you can aim a spell and cast in the same turn then you can touch and cast in the same turn? Otherwise im just going to aim all my spells at zero range and deal with the fact it has to be an area spell. I think the &quot;its a reflexive action&quot; is just an oversight and should have been stated just like with throwing spells because if it is a instant action its completely useless unless your target is immobile or its not combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-18T18:08:26-08:00","id":1177110,"title":"","content":"Best bet within the system is to Hang damaging spells which afflict whoever you're touching, with a conditional duration upon the hanging spell, that it will end when you punch someone.<br /> <br /> Just uh, don't give affectionate shoulder punches when you have such a spell hung.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T01:57:30-08:00","id":1177205,"title":"","content":"I have always interpreted the delivery of a touch spell in combat to be reflexive, especially since aimed spells are reflexive. The touch roll being penalized by Defense is a big enough penalty for me to justify it. It's just not really useful if you interpret it as not being reflexive. Even if the rules very technically specify that it's not reflexive, this is something I would house rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T02:33:54-08:00","id":1177211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1176311-combining-touch-spells-and-unarmed-attacks?p=1177205#post1177205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have always interpreted the delivery of a touch spell in combat to be reflexive, especially since aimed spells are reflexive. The touch roll being penalized by Defense is a big enough penalty for me to justify it. It's just not really useful if you interpret it as not being reflexive. Even if the rules very technically specify that it's not reflexive, this is something I would house rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you and totalgit now. It is not explicitely stated if touching in combat to deliver spells is reflexive or not. And since throwing spells is reflexive, I don't see why this should be different for basically doing the same in touching range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T09:33:15-08:00","id":1177330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1176311-combining-touch-spells-and-unarmed-attacks?p=1177205#post1177205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have always interpreted the delivery of a touch spell in combat to be reflexive, especially since aimed spells are reflexive. The touch roll being penalized by Defense is a big enough penalty for me to justify it. It's just not really useful if you interpret it as not being reflexive. Even if the rules very technically specify that it's not reflexive, this is something I would house rule.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Weirdly it doesnt penalize the touch roll by defense like it specifically does with a aimed attack. Oversight or what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T10:43:11-08:00","id":1177361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1176311-combining-touch-spells-and-unarmed-attacks?p=1177330#post1177330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Weirdly it doesnt penalize the touch roll by defense like it specifically does with a aimed attack. Oversight or what?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm gonna go out on a limb and guess that the &quot;Touching an Opponent&quot; writeup being a subheading in the &quot;Unarmed Combat&quot; section that starts a page after the book specifies the roll for a normal unarmed combat attack means it's assumed that the stat representing your ability to avoid taking a hit applies against rolls to hit you in a way that doesn't inherently deal damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T23:56:38-08:00","id":1178005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1176311-combining-touch-spells-and-unarmed-attacks?p=1177361#post1177361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm gonna go out on a limb and guess that the &quot;Touching an Opponent&quot; writeup being a subheading in the &quot;Unarmed Combat&quot; section that starts a page after the book specifies the roll for a normal unarmed combat attack means it's assumed that the stat representing your ability to avoid taking a hit applies against rolls to hit you in a way that doesn't inherently deal damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's a mistake. Touching somebody IS a lot easier, than doing actual damage with an unarmed attack. If you defend vs an unarmed attack a lot of the time arms or legs will come into contact with each other blocking a blow or likewise. If you actively try to avoid beeing touched it would be a dodging roll. Aiming a spell or throwing something at a moving target on the other hand is roughly the same, hence the same roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T03:48:46-08:00","id":1178023,"title":"","content":"Defense already represents an active avoidance of contact, just not as focused as taking the Dodge Action, same as you are supposed to be able to move your Speed without that taking your Action for the Turn, but also can use it to run. Defense penalizes &quot;Touch Attacks&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T08:33:47-08:00","id":1178083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1176311-combining-touch-spells-and-unarmed-attacks?p=1178023#post1178023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Defense already represents an active avoidance of contact, just not as focused as taking the Dodge Action, same as you are supposed to be able to move your Speed without that taking your Action for the Turn, but also can use it to run. Defense penalizes &quot;Touch Attacks&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Defense represents active avoidance of getting hurt. There is a difference. In usual melee fights a fighter will block a lot more than dodging completely out of the contact to his opponent. And when somebody is trying to block what the defender thinks is an attack, it makes sense that it is actually quite easy for the attacker to just touch that person. This is also strengthend by the fact that there is a merit like &quot;defensive combat&quot;. You don't use your weaponary skill to avoid attacks with your baton, you block them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T15:51:23-08:00","id":1178239,"title":"","content":"And that Merit lets you add Brawl or Weaponry instead of Athletics to represent precisely that. Defense still applies against touch attacks by RAW, but golden rule and all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T16:27:02-08:00","id":1178254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1176311-combining-touch-spells-and-unarmed-attacks?p=1178239#post1178239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that Merit lets you add Brawl or Weaponry instead of Athletics to represent precisely that. Defense still applies against touch attacks by RAW, but golden rule and all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going by raw it states there are 4 dice pools for an attack, str/brawl, str/weaponry, dex/firearms and dex/athletics all of which have the - defence mentioned meaning touching isnt an attack.<br /> <br /> Since touching isnt mentioned under the bold <b>Attack</b> paragraph but is situated in the <b>U</b><b><b>narmed </b>combat</b> section and which says <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">These rules present special cases that come up when fighting without weapons </span></span> </div> </div> </div>The special case is that in a fight to touch an opponent which isnt an attack the dex/brawl or weaponry (not strength for some reason) occurs without the minus to defense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 01-22-2018, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T17:02:36-08:00","id":1178274,"title":"","content":"This hugely depends on just what Defense manifests in-game. We do know that it represents instinctive ability to dodge attacks, but is it done by sidestepping away from the attack, or parrying the attack with your arms and such?<br /> <br /> Maybe we can differentiate it by having Wits-based Defense be avoiding the attack, and Dexterity-based Defense be parrying it? Just shooting in the dark here.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Or decide the means of Defense retroactively, based on the roll results. The \u201ctouch attack\u201d succeeded? Then it means the defender was trying to parry the attack with his arms, making the attacker easier to hit it. The \u201ctouch attack\u201d failed? The defender dodged the whole attack in the first place, leaving the attacker swinging at empty air.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 01-22-2018, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-22T22:26:47-08:00","id":1178366,"title":"","content":"Food for thought: delivering a touch-range spell, like any other spell, is a matter of intent and Imago. The hand is the natural delivery point for the spell, because the hand represents our primary tool for interacting with the world. So even if you deflect an attack by touching the attacker's arm, I'd still houserule that as *not* delivering the touch spell, because you need more than just &quot;any form of touch contact whatsoever.&quot; You need to touch them the way *you* intended, the way your spell's Imago demanded, in order to hit them with the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13570-amusedbyirony","name":"AmusedByIrony","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T01:35:38-08:00","id":1178387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1176311-combining-touch-spells-and-unarmed-attacks?p=1178239#post1178239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that Merit lets you add Brawl or Weaponry instead of Athletics to represent precisely that. Defense still applies against touch attacks by RAW, but golden rule and all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quote that RAW line please which clearly states that Defense applies to touching. Otherwise this is just your interpretation and I have a different one agreeing with totalgit. Defending yourself is usually a combination out of moving out of harms way and move arms or legs in front of delicate bodyparts like your head. A completely untrained person will still instinctevely move his arms in front of himself to DEFEND himself.<br /> If you actively want to avoid even getting touched in combat you can DODGE the attempt to touch you. Am I the only person thinking that these two are called Defense and Dodge on purpose? I also think it is way more interesting if touching somebody to deliver a spell is easier than trowing the spell from a distance. It's a nice trade of for getting into the heat and risking getting attacked more easily in return.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T04:32:26-08:00","id":1178403,"title":"","content":"Most of the Mage Armors that enhance Defense don\u2019t seem to improve one\u2019s ability to move one\u2019s arms to deflect attacks, though. Surely Defense can\u2019t be *all* about parrying and deflecting, as opposed to evading?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T05:00:18-08:00","id":1178407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1176311-combining-touch-spells-and-unarmed-attacks?p=1178254#post1178254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Going by raw it states there are 4 dice pools for an attack, <b>str/brawl</b>, str/weaponry, dex/firearms and dex/athletics all of which have the - defence mentioned meaning touching isnt an attack.<br /> <br /> Since touching isnt mentioned under the bold <b>Attack</b> paragraph but is situated in the <b>U</b><b><b>narmed </b>combat</b> section and which says<br /> The special case is that in a fight to touch an opponent which isnt an attack the dex/brawl or weaponry (not strength for some reason) occurs without the minus to defense.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You realize Unarmed Combat is the Str+Brawl you mentioned, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T05:04:30-08:00","id":1178408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1176311-combining-touch-spells-and-unarmed-attacks?p=1178387#post1178387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Quote that RAW line please which clearly states that Defense applies to touching. Otherwise this is just your interpretation and I have a different one agreeing with totalgit. Defending yourself is usually a combination out of moving out of harms way and move arms or legs in front of delicate bodyparts like your head. A completely untrained person will still instinctevely move his arms in front of himself to DEFEND himself.<br /> If you actively want to avoid even getting touched in combat you can DODGE the attempt to touch you. Am I the only person thinking that these two are called Defense and Dodge on purpose? I also think it is way more interesting if touching somebody to deliver a spell is easier than trowing the spell from a distance. It's a nice trade of for getting into the heat and risking getting attacked more easily in return.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Counter-offer: As applying Defense is the default and exceptions to that general rule are the ones explicitely pointed out (like in the case of most instances of Firearms), you show me where it says touch attacks are an exception that negates Defense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T05:21:35-08:00","id":1178413,"title":"","content":"Totalgit already did that but here again:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Lilith-Regular\">Touching an Opponent<br /> <span style=\"font-family:GoudyOldStyleT-Regular\">Sometimes, a combatant doesn\u2019t want to do damage. Maybe<br /> she wants to plant a bug, or deliver a touch-range spell. Roll<br /> Dexterity + Brawl, or Dexterity + Weaponry to tap an opponent<br /> with a weapon. A successful roll deals no damage</span></span></span>.<br /> <br /> P219 2e Core </div> </div> </div>I cannot read anything about applying defense. In addition: Touching is dex+brawl, which is explicetly not the brawl attack roll.<br /> Your &quot;counter-offer&quot; is simply the lazy try to imagin something that is not there. You are free to interpret the quoted paragraph the way that you subtract defense from the roll, but that is your interpretation, not what is written down there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T05:42:47-08:00","id":1178416,"title":"","content":"Fair enough, I stand corrected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T06:08:00-08:00","id":1178422,"title":"","content":"So if I pick a fight with a boxer in the back alley, and try to plant a bug on him with a touch, he won\u2019t duck and weave like he trained all the time to do, and thus I\u2019ll have an easier time than just trying to punch him?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T07:21:40-08:00","id":1178428,"title":"","content":"Apparently, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T08:11:05-08:00","id":1178437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1176311-combining-touch-spells-and-unarmed-attacks?p=1178428#post1178428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apparently, yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the difference is that its alot harder to connect with something that does damage if they are trying to avoid it than it is to just touch somebody. If two people are up close in a boxing ring, it's easy for one to touch the other even if he is &quot;ducking and weaving&quot; its much harder to actually connect a blow that causes damage (ie an attack).<br /> <br /> Defense is more the active attempt to not take damage, not the active attempt to not get touched, which as said could apply to actually dodging. Note dodging also doesnt subtract defense and if successful does no damage which is similar to trying to touch, if you dont want to be touched you dodge it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 01-23-2018, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T08:40:13-08:00","id":1178441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1176311-combining-touch-spells-and-unarmed-attacks?p=1178437#post1178437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Defense is more the active attempt to not take damage, not the active attempt to not get touched, which as said could apply to actually dodging. Note dodging also doesnt subtract defense and if successful does no damage which is similar to trying to touch, if you dont want to be touched you dodge it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's the problem: <i>there is no normal place in the mechanics where Dodge is applicable to a thing and Defense is not</i>, and in fact in the ChroD corebook copy of the mechanics <i>Dodging specifically only works when Defense can apply.</i><br /> <br /> The ChroD corebook lexicon says that Defense penalizes a close combat opponent's <i>accuracy</i>, not their <i>ability to make contact</i>, and defines &quot;close combat&quot; as attacks that involve hand-to-hand or weapon fighting, which characters gain their Defense against. Slapping a touch-of-death on a target is not <i>easier than</i> punching them in the chest for a point of bashing damage \u2014 the game simply isn't arranged such that that's an outcome that's clearly intended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T09:07:28-08:00","id":1178450,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:22px\">&quot;Touching a Target: Dexterity + Brawl or Dexterity + Weaponry; armor may or may not apply, <b>but Defense does apply.</b>&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Chronicles of Darkness, page 91<br /> <br /> Is this thread over now?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AmusedByIrony</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1176311-combining-touch-spells-and-unarmed-attacks?p=1178366#post1178366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Food for thought: delivering a touch-range spell, like any other spell, is a matter of intent and Imago. The hand is the natural delivery point for the spell, because the hand represents our primary tool for interacting with the world. So even if you deflect an attack by touching the attacker's arm, I'd still houserule that as *not* delivering the touch spell, because you need more than just &quot;any form of touch contact whatsoever.&quot; You need to touch them the way *you* intended, the way your spell's Imago demanded, in order to hit them with the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still gonna quote this because I find it to be quite a good argument as for why applying Defense against touch spells makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T10:55:46-08:00","id":1178481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1176311-combining-touch-spells-and-unarmed-attacks?p=1178450#post1178450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:22px\">&quot;Touching a Target: Dexterity + Brawl or Dexterity + Weaponry; armor may or may not apply, <b>but Defense does apply.</b>&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Chronicles of Darkness, page 91<br /> <br /> Is this thread over now?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm still gonna quote this because I find it to be quite a good argument as for why applying Defense against touch spells makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Word count is a bitch...Pretty stupid dropping that from the mage core or not adding - defense.<br /> <br /> It mentions armor, but armor will never apply since it reduces damage and touches do none. So that bit of text is irrelevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 01-23-2018, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T11:04:25-08:00","id":1178489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1176311-combining-touch-spells-and-unarmed-attacks?p=1178481#post1178481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It mentions armor, but armor will never apply since it reduces damage and touches do none. So that bit of text is irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Touch attack to attach an explosive to the opponent?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T11:13:16-08:00","id":1178491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1176311-combining-touch-spells-and-unarmed-attacks?p=1178489#post1178489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Touch attack to attach an explosive to the opponent?</div> </div> </div> </div>Attaching an explosive to somebody still does no damage at the time of the attaching though. Sure armor will help when the explosive goes off but that happens later and isnt part of the touch.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T14:01:39-08:00","id":1178542,"title":"","content":"Wait, the rule is different in the Chrod and Mage cores? Holly mess up, Batman! Well, at least there is precedent to apply Defense to touch, it didn't felt quite right to be way easier than any other type of spell delivery (althought the example of boxing being easier to hit, meaning just make contact as oppossed to land a solid blow and do damage really convinced me that it might make sense)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T15:23:08-08:00","id":1178569,"title":"","content":"It was probably a simple editing slip-up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T15:33:26-08:00","id":1178572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1176311-combining-touch-spells-and-unarmed-attacks?p=1178450#post1178450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:22px\">&quot;Touching a Target: Dexterity + Brawl or Dexterity + Weaponry; armor may or may not apply, <b>but Defense does apply.</b>&quot;</span><br /> <br /> Chronicles of Darkness, page 91<br /> <br /> Is this thread over now?</div> </div> </div> </div>What makes this more funny is that the actual detailed text in the CofD core book regarding touching an opponent does not mention defense... &quot;Sometimes, a combatant doesn\u2019t want to do damage. Maybe she wants to plant a bug, or use some supernatural power. Roll Dexterity + Brawl or Dexterity + Weaponry to tap an opponent with a weapon. A successful roll deals no damage.&quot; It's pretty easy to miss the text on page 91.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-23T23:15:56-08:00","id":1178688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>projectmoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1176311-combining-touch-spells-and-unarmed-attacks?p=1178572#post1178572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What makes this more funny is that the actual detailed text in the CofD core book regarding touching an opponent does not mention defense... &quot;Sometimes, a combatant doesn\u2019t want to do damage. Maybe she wants to plant a bug, or use some supernatural power. Roll Dexterity + Brawl or Dexterity + Weaponry to tap an opponent with a weapon. A successful roll deals no damage.&quot; It's pretty easy to miss the text on page 91.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I am actually unsure where the slip up is there. I've looked into the Werewolf core and the quick chart in CoD core is actually the only reference for applying defense. The part of armor is probably relevant if you want to touch skin or a specific part of the body which is covered.<br /> I also kind of liked the fact, that it would be easier to deliver a spell by touching rather than throwing it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1176311-combining-touch-spells-and-unarmed-attacks?p=1178441#post1178441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the problem: <i>there is no normal place in the mechanics where Dodge is applicable to a thing and Defense is not</i>, and in fact in the ChroD corebook copy of the mechanics <i>Dodging specifically only works when Defense can apply.</i><br /> <br /> The ChroD corebook lexicon says that Defense penalizes a close combat opponent's <i>accuracy</i>, not their <i>ability to make contact</i>, and defines &quot;close combat&quot; as attacks that involve hand-to-hand or weapon fighting, which characters gain their Defense against. Slapping a touch-of-death on a target is not <i>easier than</i> punching them in the chest for a point of bashing damage \u2014 the game simply isn't arranged such that that's an outcome that's clearly intended.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there really not a single incident where you HAVE to use dodge? Like a rampaging elephant or explosions or something? Because if so, Dodge is completely useless. Mathematically it is always better to substract your Defense from an enemy roll instead of rolling double Defense yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","user":"HardcoreHannes","date":". 01-24-2018, 02:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T05:12:11-08:00","id":1178728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1176311-combining-touch-spells-and-unarmed-attacks?p=1178688#post1178688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mathematically it is always better to substract your Defense from an enemy roll instead of rolling double Defense yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're wrong. If your Defense is half your opponents attack dice pool, you remove half of the expected successes. If you double that Defense and roll it you'll get on average the same amount of successes as your opponent, meaning you're likely to completely negate the attack, and even when you don't you're still much more likely to remove more successes than your Defense would remove expected successes.<br /> <br /> Edit: Another simple way of handling it is looking at how many successes Defense and Dodge removes. Defense removes 1/3 successes per point, since each die grants an average of ~1/3 successes. Dodge rolls two dice per point of Defense, so each point equals around 2/3 successes, and removes the same amount of successes. This means Dodge is literally twice as effective, barring circumstances where the opponent applies dice tricks to their attack, in which the effect of Defense increases slightly but far from enough for it to be more effective than dodging.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 01-24-2018, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count